<div class="clearfix lb-extra-spacing"></div>

<span class="new-centered-article-text">
    The Camp Hero Vest took a good amount on tinkering to get to wear it is now. During early stage development we had sampled it in our crinkle nylon from the Effo short but the fabric made the vest feel too casual, maybe even a bit too retro for what we had in our heads. By using the 90/10 4 way stretch fabric which can also be found on the soon to be rereleased Camp Hero Short, we were able to keep the exterior of the vest and the overall appearance clean. The front and back yolk seams are barely noticeable with a clean single top stitch. 
    <br><br>
    Zippered hand pockets are hidden behind an opening that floats along both front side seams. Our chest pocket was designed with running in mind so a cell phone or keys aren’t bouncing around near your waistline.  Not having the chest pocket set into the garment helps with reducing zipper snags. We’re quite happy with the initial development of the Camp Hero Vest and already have it placed in upcoming seasons which gives us the opportunity to continue to tinker with the design and take it new levels.
</span>

