</div>

<span class="new-centered-article-text">
    Calipers are measuring devices or the “squeezers” on modern disc brakes. Thinking back on it, we’re not sure why we named to Caliper Jacket after a car brake component. Maybe it has to do with having the ability to stop light wind and rain. Our Caliper Jacket looks like a simple sew on the inside of the jacket but in order to get a clean interior finish with french seams things basically have to be folded and stitched twice. French seam construction adds more water repellency to a jacket but can’t keep out high pressure water exposure like sitting in a snow bunker for hours or getting sprayed by a fire hose.
</span>

